==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|mouch}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|moochen}}, {{m|enm|mouchen|t=to pretend poverty}}, from {{der|en|fro|muchier}}, {{m|fro|mucier}}, {{m|fro|mucer|t=to skulk, hide, conceal}}, from {{der|en|frk|*mukjan|t=to hide, conceal oneself}}, from {{der|en|gem-pro|*mūk-|*mukjaną}}, {{m|gem-pro|*mūk-|*mūkōną|t=to hide, ambush}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*(s)mūg-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*(s)mewgʰ-|t=swindler, thief}}.

Cognate with {{cog|goh|mūhhōn|t=to store, cache, plunder}}, {{cog|gmh|muchen}}, {{m|gmh|mucken|t=to hide, stash}}, {{cog|enm|muchen|müchen}}, {{m|enm|michen|t=to rob, steal, pilfer}}. More at {{l|en|mitch}}.

Alternate etymology derives ''mooch'' from {{inh|en|enm|mucchen|t=to hoard, be stingy|lit=to hide coins in one's nightcap}}, from {{der|en|enm|mucche|t=nightcap}}, from {{der|en|dum|mutse|t=cap, nightcap}}, from {{der|en|ML.|almucia|t=nightcap}}, of unknown origin, possibly Arabic. More at {{l|en|mutch}}, {{l|en|amice}}.

